abstract: >-
  RNSpectraX is a browser-based suite for processing, analysing and plotting
  Raman/SERS spectra and general XY data. It provides despiking, baseline
  correction (ModPoly, rubber band, rolling ball, asymmetric least squares),
  smoothing, normalisation, shift calibration and derivative spectra; group
  statistics; peak detection and band assignment; reference-library
  identification; band fitting, band ratios with significance tests, PCA and
  difference spectra; least-squares curve fitting; and resonance tracking
  with calibration, LOD and LOQ for SPR/LSPR sensing. All calculations run
  locally in the browser.
keywords:
  - Raman spectroscopy
  - SERS
  - spectral analysis
  - baseline correction
  - peak fitting
  - principal component analysis
  - curve fitting
  - surface plasmon resonance
  - scientific plotting
  - photonics
